  "live_records": {
    "q-20053": {
      "dom_id": "step-q20053",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨-2,2,-3⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,2⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,1,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c).$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2)-2(2\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2)-3(2\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =6-12+0 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
