    "q-20062": {
      "dom_id": "step-q20062",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $b\\times c=⟨2,3,0⟩$ and $a=⟨1,-2,2⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨1,-2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2-6+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
