    "q-73462": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73462",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $p=⟨3,1,2⟩$, $q=⟨1,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,1,-2⟩.$ Find $r\\cdot (q\\times p).$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the scalar triple product $r\\cdot (q\\times p)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $r,$ $q,$ and $p.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot (q\\times p) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3)-2(1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-20+1-14 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
