    "q-317318": {
      "dom_id": "step-q317318",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨-1,2,4⟩$, $b=⟨0,3,1⟩$ and $c=⟨2,5,0⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\,(3\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 5)\\,-\\,2\\,(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2)\\,+\\,4\\,(0\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =(-1)\\,(-5)\\,-\\,2\\,(-2)\\,+\\,4\\,(-6) \\\\  & =5+4-24 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
